    {
      "action": "update",
      "nodeId": "d77/rotational-classification-scope",
      "parentId": "program/rotational-symmetry",
      "nodeType": "claim",
      "title": "Arbitrary-center rotational classification and its scope",
      "summary": "A nonidentity Euclidean rotation preserving a finite noncollinear subset of Z², about an arbitrary center, must be a half-turn or quarter-turn. Hence a hypothetical 153-point no-three-in-line subset of G_77 has no nonidentity rotational symmetry, while rotational symmetry at cardinality 154 must be the centered half-turn described by the companion lemma. This does not classify reflections or identify all centered half-turn configurations with rct4.",
