    {
      "action": "update",
      "nodeId": "rotational-symmetry/cardinality-obstructions",
      "parentId": "program/rotational-symmetry",
      "nodeType": "lemma",
      "title": "Half-turn and quarter-turn cardinality obstructions",
      "summary": "Every nonidentity Euclidean rotation preserving a finite noncollinear lattice set is a half-turn or quarter-turn. The accepted orbit obstructions therefore exclude all nonidentity rotational symmetry for a hypothetical 153-point no-three-in-line subset of G_77 and imply that any rotational symmetry at cardinality 154 must be a half-turn. These conclusions do not assert nonexistence or classify reflections.",
